From 09a67c0723087f8d26ad7f2b230103366a215e3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PhillipT1 <43970944+PhillipT1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:44:57 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] Make StorageEngine commits and page eviction write-ahead safe

- Buffer pool for StorageEngine is no-steal: eviction never writes a dirty,
  uncommitted page to the device. A write that needs one fails with
  UncommittedPagesPinned before anything is logged.
- commit() is replaced by commit_durable(persist): the commit marker is
  appended, the complete log is persisted, and only then are pages flushed.
  If persist fails the marker is withdrawn.
- write_page checks bounds and reserves a frame before logging, and withdraws
  its log record if staging fails, so a failed write can never become durable
  through a later commit.
- Tests: refused eviction leaves the device and log untouched; data is not
  flushed before the log is persisted; a failed persist withdraws the marker;
  out-of-bounds writes are refused before logging.
